  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Generation Garment Factory Owners Need assessment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh&apos;s apparel and textile industry has achieved significant success as a global garments manufacturer, but at a high environmental cost. The industry&apos;s exponential growth has resulted in substantial waste generation, resource depletion and pollution. Embracing circular economy principles offers a compelling solution to these challenges by transitioning from a linear model to one that promotes resource efficiency and waste reduction.The purpose of this project is to increase awareness and a sense of urgency amongst members of the Bangladesh Apparel Youth Leaders Association (BAYLA) regarding circular economy principals for the ready-made garments industry and to conduct a need assessment among BAYLA-members on the possible circular economy knowledge/technology gap they experience.The need assessment will be used to draft a concrete proposal for a circular textile executive knowledge and trading platform that can provide concrete solutions to overcome existing gaps for the next generation garment factory owners.</narrative>
  </description>
